  "description": "Organizing — the social-scale reading of `governing`: the settling of an open plurality of agents into one bounded, law-bearing collective (community → institution → polity). It is the Gen-2 (inter-agent) lift of @emsenn/animating along the agency spiral: where animating glues three faculty-faces into one agent, organizing glues a sheaf of agents into one organization. A holographic sheaf-gluing node at the social scale — base = a sheaf of agents over a social base; three Gen-2 boundary faces (socializing across, computing inside, gaming outside); interior bulk = the organization (the global section). The gluing act is `adjudication` (the receiving dual of speaking): it holds many agents' contributions into one record-state under three disciplines — conflict held contested (Belnap), partial held open, accumulation monotone and converging without requiring every source to coordinate — so H¹ over the social cover is the consensus cost (zero = coordination-free, non-zero = adjudication required). The operations chain (task→work→assign→office→consensus→federation) is organizing's downstream content, not its essence; this package is the binder. See dev/docs/notes/2026-06-21-organizing-as-social-scale-governing.md.",
  "engines": {
    "node": ">=22.18"
  },
  "scripts": {
    "clean": "rm -rf dist .tmp",
    "check": "tsc --noEmit && tsc -p tsconfig.scripts.json --noEmit",
    "build": "tsc -p tsconfig.build.json && tsc -p tsconfig.scripts.json && node copy-dist-assets.mjs && chmod +x dist/scripts/*.mjs",
    "test": "pnpm run build && node --test \"test/*.test.mjs\"",
    "verify": "pnpm run check && pnpm run build",
    "rebuild": "pnpm run clean && pnpm run build",
    "examples": "node examples/organize.mjs"
  },
  "main": "./dist/index.mjs",
  "types": "./dist/index.d.mts",
  "bin": {
    "organize": "./dist/scripts/cli.mjs",
    "organize-serve": "./dist/scripts/serve.mjs"
  },
